["er.request/1",{"arguments":{"body":"# Core contracts and integration\n\nOperator approved stages 1–3 and 7 on 2026-09-28. Canonical typed declarations validate in `ess/ess-inputs.yaml`. Reuse the existing service and recording coordinates, retain legacy entrypoints, and keep the binding inventory diagnostic.\n\n## Scope\n\nOwn shared `ess/ess-inputs.yaml`, `ess/system.yaml`, core domain/component/scenarios, standalone `checks/ess-conformance` runner/helpers/manifest/lockfile, reviewed coverage baseline, traceability register, local/CI gate integration and authority adoption only after full conformance. Other implementation units exclusively own shell/query and store/executor adapters and domain inputs in their managed worktrees. ESS direct-return observation is a separately governed upstream story.\n\n## Acceptance scenarios\n\nCore: invalid definitions/reference scopes/defaults/accumulated errors; registration and versions; creation and execution refusal precedence/preconditions/invariants; service/1 selection and identity; service/2 presence; service/3 field fulfillment and derived identity; exact numbers; ordered duplicate/zero events; deterministic decisions and replay/tamper across all four record formats.\nIntegration: admit original suite bytes; run real library ConformanceTargets; retain report/2 and model/source identity; fail all nonpasses and refusals; require exact reviewed scenario inventory; regenerate canonical IR/suites twice identically; preserve production dependency boundaries and MSRV; deliberately mutate behavior per domain and observe named failures; full task check and AEP validation before claiming conforming.\n\n## Baseline evidence\n\nBoth legacy coordinate manifests validate and compile on ESS 0.37.0. The canonical five-domain manifest validates (13 inputs). Scoped cargo tests across all five crates exited 0; log retained outside build output at `task-local-retained-evidence` pending evidence integration. No behavior changes are authorized by this specification effort. Native Binary64 and pure return-value observation limitations have retained reproducers; no weaker substitute is counted as native typed support.\n","document":{"events":[{"args":{"changes":{"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":".github/workflows/gate.yml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Taskfile.yml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/core.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/main.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/target.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/domains/core.yaml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/ess-inputs.yaml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/scenarios/core"}]},"command":"update-entity","target":"ent-5aa9cdc15c562f541365f863a4f3b7f9"},"changed":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":1790561181193,"id":"ent-5aa9cdc15c562f541365f863a4f3b7f9","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/er-core-conformance-integration","provenance":{"created_by":"human:timo","updated_by":"human:timo"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":1790561252941}},"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":".github/workflows/gate.yml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Taskfile.yml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/core.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/main.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/target.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/domains/core.yaml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/ess-inputs.yaml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/scenarios/core"}]},"entity":"aep.entity","from_state":"active","id":"ent-5aa9cdc15c562f541365f863a4f3b7f9","payload":{"actor":"human:timo","at":1790561252941,"causation":"cmd-child-3993e77269b3af4189f7aca90ca5304a5e49111a1ae69ba37af0c400e367c623","correlation":"protocol-artifact-scope","event_id":"aep.entity:ent-5aa9cdc15c562f541365f863a4f3b7f9@4#0~834982b9fceef40f","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-28T02:07:32Z"},"revision":4,"to_state":"ac